# Exclusions for the `make test-isolation` build context (see the Makefile
# target's own comment and this directory's Dockerfile). NOT the same file as
# the repo-root .dockerignore: that one excludes test/ entirely (fine for the
# production sqi-server image, fatal here — this image needs
# test/integration/**). The Makefile stages a filtered copy of the repo using
# these patterns rather than relying on Docker's own per-context .dockerignore
# discovery, since two different Dockerfiles sharing the repo root as context
# cannot each have their own automatically-selected ignore file with the
# classic (non-BuildKit) builder this project's Docker install runs.
#
# Patterns follow rsync --exclude-from syntax (used by the Makefile target),
# not Docker's own .dockerignore glob dialect. Unlike .git/ and node_modules/
# above, the entries below are untracked LOCAL dev artifacts — nothing here
# affects CI or a fresh clone, since neither ever has them — but staging them
# anyway wastes real time and disk on every `make test-isolation` run on a
# machine that has run docs tooling or the Python clients' test suites: a
# multi-gigabyte venv or mypy cache gets rsync'd into the build context and
# then immediately excluded a second time (COPY . . in the Dockerfile only
# needs go.mod's own module tree plus test/integration/), for no benefit.
.git/
web/node_modules/
bin/
.superpowers/
.venv-docs/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
coverage/
# Anchored (leading /, matching this file's own rsync --exclude-from
# semantics — NOT a bare "dist/", which would also match web/dist/: that
# directory is load-bearing, holding the git-tracked index.html placeholder
# //go:embed dist (web/embed.go) requires to compile even before a web build
# has run. These two are the actual local Python build-artifact dist dirs,
# mirroring the repo-root .gitignore's own /clients/python/dist/ entry.
/clients/python/dist/
/clients/submitter/dist/
